+  <div class="rodd-head">
+    <span class="rodd-title">Sizing</span>
+    <span class="rodd-fig">3,159%</span>
+  </div>
+  <p class="rodd-why"><b>RoDD is the metric this catalog is priced on.</b> Net profit divided by the worst
+  peak-to-valley drawdown: this system&rsquo;s window (16 months) returned
+  <b>3,159%</b> on its drawdown. Shown at Multiplier 5; one multiple draws down
+  <b>$2,766</b> at worst (full record).</p>
+  <p class="ro-lead">This amount is your DRAWDOWN BUDGET, not your account size.</p>
+  <p class="ro-warn">We recommend the drawdown never exceeds 25% of your account balance (a $2,500 drawdown budget means a $10,000 account or more). Raising the Multiplier raises profit and drawdown together and is inherently risky.</p>
+  <input type="radio" name="ro-aftershock" id="ro-aftershock-1" class="ro-r ro-red"><input type="radio" name="ro-aftershock" id="ro-aftershock-2" class="ro-r ro-ok" checked><input type="radio" name="ro-aftershock" id="ro-aftershock-3" class="ro-r ro-amb"><input type="radio" name="ro-aftershock" id="ro-aftershock-4" class="ro-r ro-ok"><input type="radio" name="ro-aftershock" id="ro-aftershock-5" class="ro-r ro-ok">
