+  <div class="ro-outs"><div class="ro-out ro-out-1"><span class="ro-flag">Not built for this size</span> One multiple of this system draws down <b>$2,766</b> at worst (full record) &mdash; more than a $2.5k drawdown budget covers. The smallest budget that holds 1&times; is $5,000.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-2"><span class="ro-flag ro-flag-rec">Recommended</span> Fits at <b>1&times;</b> (of the published 5&times;). One multiple draws down <b>$2,766</b> at worst (full record); 1&times; uses about <b>$2,766</b> of a $5k budget. Expected average monthly profit at 1&times;: <b class="ro-ret">&asymp;$3,399</b> (best window, 15.6 months; $3,399 per multiple). Past results, not a forecast.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-3"><span class="ro-flag">Thin cushion</span> 3&times; leaves under a quarter of this budget spare after its worst published drawdown. <span class="ro-flag ro-flag-rec">Fits at 3&times;</span> Fits at <b>3&times;</b> (of the published 5&times;). One multiple draws down <b>$2,766</b> at worst (full record); 3&times; uses about <b>$8,300</b> of a $10k budget. Expected average monthly profit at 3&times;: <b class="ro-ret">&asymp;$10,198</b> (best window, 15.6 months; $3,399 per multiple). Past results, not a forecast.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-4"><span class="ro-flag ro-flag-rec">Fits at 5&times;</span> Fits at <b>5&times;</b> (the full published size). One multiple draws down <b>$2,766</b> at worst (full record); 5&times; uses about <b>$13,832</b> of a $25k budget. Expected average monthly profit at 5&times;: <b class="ro-ret">&asymp;$16,996</b> (best window, 15.6 months; $3,399 per multiple). Past results, not a forecast.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-5"><span class="ro-flag ro-flag-rec">Fits at 5&times;</span> Fits at <b>5&times;</b> (the full published size). One multiple draws down <b>$2,766</b> at worst (full record); 5&times; uses about <b>$13,832</b> of a $50k budget. Expected average monthly profit at 5&times;: <b class="ro-ret">&asymp;$16,996</b> (best window, 15.6 months; $3,399 per multiple). Past results, not a forecast. This budget exceeds the published 5&times; size; we do not recommend raising the Multiplier beyond it &mdash; profit and drawdown rise together.</div></div>
+  <p class="ro-note">Fit multiplier = drawdown budget &divide; one multiple&rsquo;s worst published drawdown, capped at the published Multiplier. Linear scaling of the published window; not a projection of future results.</p>
