st window, 15.9 months; $427 per multiple). Past results, not a forecast. This budget exceeds the published 18&times; size; we do not recommend raising the Multiplier beyond it &mdash; profit and drawdown rise together.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-5"><span class="ro-flag ro-flag-rec">Fits at 18&times;</span> Fits at <b>18&times;</b> (the full published size). One multiple draws down <b>$540</b> at worst (best window); 18&times; uses about <b>$9,720</b> of a $50k budget. Expected average monthly profit at 18&times;: <b class="ro-ret">&asymp;$7,678</b> (best window, 15.9 months; $427 per multiple). Past results, not a forecast. This budget exceeds the published 18&times; size; we do not recommend raising the Multiplier beyond it &mdash; profit and drawdown rise together.</div></div>
