ommend raising the Multiplier beyond it &mdash; profit and drawdown rise together.</div><div class="ro-out ro-out-5"><span class="ro-flag ro-flag-rec">Fits at 3&times;</span> Fits at <b>3&times;</b> (the full published size). One multiple draws down <b>$2,332</b> at worst (best window); 3&times; uses about <b>$6,996</b> of a $50k budget. Expected average monthly profit at 3&times;: <b class="ro-ret">&asymp;$12,332</b> (best window, 8 months; $4,111 per multiple). Past results, not a forecast. This budget exceeds the published 3&times; size; we do not recommend raising the Multiplier beyond it &mdash; profit and drawdown rise together.</div></div>
